#!/usr/bin/env perl

use strict;
use warnings;

# Grab --pt-config before Mojolicious sees the argv, then pass the rest through.
use Getopt::Long qw(:config pass_through);
GetOptions( 'pt-config=s' => \( my $pt_config ) );
$ENV{NISABA_CONFIG} = $pt_config if defined $pt_config;

use Mojolicious::Commands;
Mojolicious::Commands->start_app('App::Nisaba::WebSelfService');

=head1 NAME

mojo_nisaba_selfservice - Self-service web portal for App::Nisaba

=head1 SYNOPSIS

  # Development server (port 3000)
  mojo_nisaba_selfservice daemon

  # Custom port
  mojo_nisaba_selfservice daemon -l http://*:8081

  # Production (prefork)
  mojo_nisaba_selfservice prefork -l http://*:8081

  # With a custom nisaba config
  mojo_nisaba_selfservice daemon --pt-config /etc/nisabarc

=head1 DESCRIPTION

Starts the App::Nisaba self-service web interface. Users can log in
with their LDAP credentials to change their password and manage SSH
public keys.

All standard Mojolicious server commands (C<daemon>, C<prefork>, etc.)
are supported after any C<--pt-config> argument.

=head1 ENVIRONMENT

=head2 NISABA_CONFIG

Path to the nisabarc config file. Overridden by C<--pt-config>.

=head2 NISABA_SECRET

Session secret. Set this to a long random string in production.

=head1 CONFIG KEYS (nisabarc)

In addition to the standard App::Nisaba LDAP settings, the following
keys control email-based password reset:

=head2 smtpserver

Hostname of the SMTP relay. Required to enable password reset emails.

=head2 smtpfrom

From address used when sending password reset emails. Required.

=head2 smtpport

SMTP port number. Defaults to C<25>.

=head2 smtptls

Enable TLS for SMTP. Set to C<ssl> for implicit TLS (SMTPS, typically
port 465) or C<starttls> for explicit STARTTLS (typically port 587).
Leave unset or empty for plain SMTP. Requires C<IO::Socket::SSL>.

=head2 smtpuser

SMTP authentication username. Optional.

=head2 smtppass

SMTP authentication password. Optional (requires C<smtpuser>).

=head1 SEE ALSO

L<App::Nisaba>, L<App::Nisaba::WebSelfService>

=cut
